{"final":{"answer":"The reserve for product warranties rose from $4 million at the end of 2005 to $10 million at the end of 2006, a net increase of $6 million. The disclosed 2006 activity supports this: $4 million of pretax warranty charges, less $5 million of cash outlays, plus $7 million of warranty obligations assumed in 2006 acquisitions, giving a +$6 million net change, which reconciles with the beginning and ending reserve balances.","value":6,"unit":"USD_million","sources":["source:q11n3","source:q11n4","source:q12n3","source:q13n0","source:q14n0"],"result_id":"tool:1"}}